    "entrance": "Safe lower well with a lantern and an upper rim.",
    "exit": "Upper sunlit passage.",
    "solution": "Pick up the lantern and jump beside the step. Throw it into the step face, dash upward with free hands, then hold Grab during the rise to retrieve it. The catch preserves the upward dash speed and lifts the lantern onto the rim. Carry it past the overhead beam. An ordinary carrying jump or an unaccompanied upward dash cannot deliver the shade.",
    "nearestExisting": "No Place to Land trades a lantern for an extra feather jump. This uses the new dash catch to reconnect an object to an already-moving knight: the object is briefly released to permit the ascent, then its return does not cancel the upward velocity.",
    "novelty": "The full-hands restriction becomes an ordering problem. Separate cargo and knight for one action, then recover both upward momentum and shade. A failed ascent falls into a safe well, so the transfer can be retried without a lethal precision penalty.",
